  "context_pill": "Tax Liability Computation (Old Regime)",
  "example_summary": "Calculating tax for a resident individual (income ₹ 4,15,000) who opts out of the default regime to use the old tax slabs and Section 87A rebate.",
  "source_provision": "| Statutory Provision | Eligibility Criteria | Threshold Limit | Tax Rate / Rebate Amount |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Option u/s 115BAC(6)** | Individual / HUF / AOP / BOI / AJP | Opting out of Default Regime | Applies Normal Tax Rates (Old Regime) |\n| **Basic Exemption Limit (Old Regime)** | Resident Individual aged < 60 years | Income up to ₹ 2,50,000 | **Nil** |\n| **First Slab Rate (Old Regime)** | Resident Individual aged < 60 years | Income ₹ 2,50,001 to ₹ 5,00,000 | **5%** |\n| **Section 87A Rebate (Old Regime)** | Resident Individual Only | Total Income ≤ ₹ 5,00,000 | Lower of **100% of tax** or **₹ 12,500** |\n\n### Core Statutory Rules\n\n* **Option to Shift Out u/s 115BAC(6)**: An individual without business income can exercise the option to shift out of the default tax regime under Section 115BAC on a year-to-year basis while filing the return u/s 139(1).\n\n* **Section 87A Rebate Applicability**: Available exclusively to **Resident Individuals** when Total Income does not cross **₹ 5,00,000** under the optional old tax regime.\n\n> [!NOTE] Health and Education Cess:\n> Health and Education Cess @ 4% is calculated on the net income tax payable **after** deducting the rebate u/s 87A. If tax payable post-rebate is Nil, no Cess applies.",
